    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Created by the Bolsheviks in the October Revolution of 1917, it was the world’s first state committed to building socialism.</li><li>It won the Civil War and in 1922 co-founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, holding about three-quarters of its territory.</li><li>In 1990–1991 it declared <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sovereignty">sovereignty</a>, elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#boris-yeltsin">Boris Yeltsin</a> president and became the Russian Federation.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The largest Soviet republic was the only one without its own Communist Party until 1990: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#moscow">Moscow</a> feared that a Russian party would become a rival centre of power to the Union party.</p></aside>
    </section>

